539	+
540	+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
541	+
542	+**Goal:** `ModelTurnAccumulator::finish()` fails with a clear `ambiguous tool calls:` error when two or more name-carrying deltas arrive under `call_id: ""`, instead of merging them.
543	+
544	+**Architecture:** `observe` counts name-carrying deltas under `""` and keeps their names. `finish()` checks that count before it parses any arguments. Then the docs, the litellm pinning test and conformance assertion 7 change to match.
545	+
546	+**Tech Stack:** Rust 1.94, `serde_json`, `tracing` (already a `core` dependency).
547	+
548	+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-21-blank-call-id-accumulator-design.md`
549	+
550	+## Global Constraints
551	+
552	+- No public signature change. `finish()` stays `pub fn finish(self) -> Result<ModelTurn, String>`.
553	+- No hand-bumped crate version and no CHANGELOG edit. release-plz does both.
554	+- Error prefix, exactly: `ambiguous tool calls:`.
555	+- Names in the message and the warn: `{:?}` formatted, at most 8 listed then `and N more`, each cut to 64 characters before formatting. Never argument text.
556	+- `Some("")` counts as a name. Equal names count separately.
557	+- Count 0 or 1 under `""`, and every non-blank id: behaviour stays exactly as on `main`.
558	+- Commit format: `<type>(<scope>): SMA-621 <lowercase subject>`. Scopes used here: `core` and `providers` (`tests` is not in the `.versionrc` allowlist). Stage explicit paths only, never `git add -A` (`.env` is not ignored).
