807	+# SMA-621: refuse parallel blank-`call_id` tool calls in `ModelTurnAccumulator`
808	+
809	+Status: draft for approval (revised after the adversarial spec challenge).
810	+Size: small change. The behaviour change is in `core`. The other edits are docs and
811	+tests in `providers-litellm`, `runtime-temporal` and the conformance suite.
812	+
813	+## Intent
814	+
815	+`ModelTurnAccumulator::observe` groups `ToolCallDelta`s by `call_id`
816	+(`core/src/model.rs:594-600`). It does not exempt the blank id `""`. So N parallel
817	+calls that arrive under `""` become one `Item::ToolCall`. The first name wins and the
818	+arguments of all calls concatenate. On `main` this has three outcomes:
819	+
820	+1. **Loud, wrong cause.** Two calls carry arguments. The concatenation
821	+   (`{"p":1}{"q":2}`) fails to parse. `finish()` returns a `serde_json` "trailing
822	+   characters" error, and the run fails with no statement of the real cause.
823	+2. **Silent loss.** Two calls carry no arguments. `finish()` returns `Ok` with one
824	+   call. The second call is lost and nothing reports it.
825	+3. **Silent misattribution.** The first call carries no arguments and the second
826	+   call does: `("", Some("delete_all"), "")`, then `("", Some("search"), "{\"q\":1}")`.
827	+   The joined text parses. `finish()` returns `Ok`, and **`delete_all` runs with
828	+   `search`'s arguments**. Both chat translators can emit this shape: a delta with no
829	+   name fragment flushes the name with empty arguments (`openai/chat.rs:842-849`,
830	+   `providers-litellm/src/stream.rs:580-587`).
831	+
832	+The goal: the accumulator must never guess, and a failure must name the real cause.
833	+
834	+No blank-id capture exists in the repo (SMA-616 spec), and no known backend is
835	+recorded as one that sends `"id": ""`. So the effect of outcomes 2 and 3 changing
836	+from `Ok` to `Err` on real users is not known. `ModelSettings` has no
837	+`parallel_tool_calls` setting (`model.rs:137-157`), so a user who hits the new error
838	+has no workaround in this crate.
839	+
840	+## Decision (acceptance criterion 1)
841	+
842	+The ticket offers options 1, 2 and 3. Sven picked "Approach A" on 2026-11-21. It is a
843	+`core`-only form of ticket option 2.
844	+
845	+| Row | Ticket option | What it does | Result and reason |
846	+|-----|---------------|--------------|-------------------|
