852	+
853	+Ticket option 2 refuses **every** blank-id call and needs every translator to change.
854	+Approach A refuses only the ambiguous case. A single blank-id call keeps its current
855	+behaviour.
856	+
857	+## Design
858	+
859	+### Contract
860	+
861	+The `ModelEvent::ToolCallDelta` doc comment (`model.rs:183-197`) now states the
862	+invariant that the detection needs: **each blank-id call carries exactly one
863	+name-carrying delta**. It says today only that two such calls "each carry a name".
864	+All six translators already comply. The challenge checked each one: litellm once per
865	+key, openai/chat once per index, openai/responses once per item, anthropic and
866	+bedrock once per block, gemini once per part. This is a doc change to the contract
867	+that records the current behaviour. It does not change what any translator emits.
868	+
869	+### Detection
870	+
871	+- `ModelTurnAccumulator` counts the deltas with `name: Some(_)` that it observes
872	+  under `call_id == ""`, and keeps those names in arrival order.
873	+- `Some("")` counts. It is a name-carrying delta. No translator emits it today.
874	+- Equal names count separately. `"alpha"`, `"alpha"` are two calls under the
875	+  contract, so the count does not de-duplicate.
876	+- A count of 0 or 1 keeps the current behaviour exactly: the deltas merge into one
877	+  bucket and the item has `call_id: ""`.
878	+- Non-blank ids keep the current behaviour exactly, including first-name-wins.
879	+
880	+### Failure
881	+
882	+- `finish()` checks for the ambiguous case **before** it parses any arguments, for
883	+  every bucket. So the ambiguity error replaces any `serde_json` error in the same
884	+  turn, and outcomes 2 and 3 fail too.
885	+- The whole turn fails, also when a valid non-blank call is in the same turn and
886	+  assistant text is present. That is the same outcome as today's outcome 1. Keeping
887	+  the text and dropping the calls would hand the loop a turn that silently lost its
888	+  tool calls, which is the class of defect this change removes.
889	+- The return type stays `Result<ModelTurn, String>`. No public signature changes.
890	+- The message starts with the stable prefix `ambiguous tool calls:`. Then it gives the
891	+  count and the names. Proposed text:
892	+  `ambiguous tool calls: 2 parallel tool calls arrived under a blank call_id (names: "alpha", "beta"); their arguments cannot be attributed to a call`.
893	+- Message constraints. Tool names come from the model, and the message reaches
894	+  clients through `AgentEvent::RunFailed` (`agent.rs:1514`) and AG-UI.
895	+  - Format each name with `{:?}`, so control characters are escaped.
896	+  - List at most 8 names, then write `and N more`. Cut each name at 64 characters.
897	+  - Never put argument text in the message. Arguments can contain secrets.
898	+- `finish()` also writes a `tracing::warn!` with the count and the names (same
899	+  constraints). The reason: `agent.rs:1511-1512` records only
900	+  `otel.status_code = ERROR` on the span, not the message. `core` already depends
901	+  on `tracing`.
902	+- Callers need no change. `agent.rs:1508-1516` turns the `Err` into
903	+  `AgentError::Other` and `RunFailed { error }`. `runtime-temporal`
904	+  (`activities.rs:97-111`) turns it into `ErrorKindPayload::Other`, which is a
905	+  non-retryable failure (`activities.rs:265-269`). `RetryingModel` retries only
906	+  before the first event (`runtime-tokio/src/retry.rs:133-137`), so a retry cannot
907	+  replay deltas into a false positive.
908	+
909	+### Limits (accepted residual shapes)
910	+
911	+Approach A is correct only for streams that obey the contract above. Two shapes from a
912	+malformed backend remain, and this change accepts both:
913	+
914	+- **False positive.** A backend moves one blank-id call across two wire keys (in
915	+  chat, two `index` values; `canonicalize` does not alias them because it returns
916	+  early for `""` at `chat.rs:552-561`). Two names go out for one call. Today that
917	+  call can return `Ok`. After the change it returns the ambiguity error. A loud
918	+  failure on a malformed stream is acceptable.
919	+- **False negative.** A nameless blank-id call (for example the litellm cross-key
920	+  split described at `chat.rs:686-690`) merges with one named call. The count is 1,
921	+  so detection does not fire, and the named tool can run with the other call's
922	+  arguments. The cause is a translator defect, not an accumulator defect. It stays
923	+  out of scope.
924	+
925	+## Updates
926	+
927	+1. **New `core` tests** in `model.rs` `model_turn_tests`. Each test that changes
928	+   behaviour must FAIL on `main` first (acceptance criterion 3), and its doc comment
929	+   says "Confirmed to FAIL against `main`", as the repo already does
930	+   (`litellm stream.rs:2162-2165`).
931	+   - Two blank-id calls with distinct arguments: `Err`, and the message starts with
932	+     `ambiguous tool calls:` and contains both names. (`main`: a `serde_json` error.)
933	+   - Two blank-id calls with no arguments: `Err`. (`main`: `Ok`.)
934	+   - Outcome 3, misattribution: `Err`. (`main`: `Ok` with the wrong arguments.)
935	+   - Equal names (`alpha`, `alpha`): `Err`. This kills a mutant that de-duplicates.
936	+   - An ambiguous `""` bucket plus a valid `c1` call: `Err` for the whole turn.
937	+   - An ambiguous `""` bucket plus invalid JSON under `c1`: the ambiguity error, not
938	+     the JSON error. This pins "check before parse".
939	+   - The message does not contain argument text.
940	+   - Controls that pass on `main` and after the change: one blank-id call gives one
